<|channel>thought
<channel|>Password recovery is a classic tug-of-war between convenience and control. When you opt for "magic links" or SMS codes, you gain seamless access and avoid the headache of forgotten strings of characters. It’s frictionless. 

However, that ease comes at a cost to your security perimeter. Every recovery shortcut is a potential backdoor for an attacker. The more ways you have to bypass a password, the more surface area you create for a breach. We have to decide: do we want life to be easier, or do we want it to be harder to hack? [end of text]


